<section class="n-bg-paper n-pad-sm" id="unincorporated" aria-labelledby="unin-h" style="border-top:1px solid var(--n-rule);border-bottom:1px solid var(--n-rule)">
<div class="n-wrap">
<div class="n-two">
<div>
<div class="n-label">The short version</div>
<h2 class="n-h2" id="unin-h" style="margin-top:12px;max-width:20ch;color:var(--n-evergreen)">There is no mayor, and no town hall</h2>
</div>
<div class="n-read">
<p class="n-body" style="margin:0">Niwot is a census designated place in unincorporated Boulder County. It has never been an incorporated municipality, so it has no mayor, no council, no town clerk and no municipal offices. The 2020 census recorded 4,306 people living in it.</p>
<p class="n-body" style="margin:18px 0 0">In practice that means two things. Public services come from the county and from a set of special districts, each responsible for one thing &#8212; water from one district, sewer from another, fire from a third, schools from a fourth, roads and permits from the county. And everything that is not a public service &#8212; the events, the sculpture park, the flower baskets, the sense that anything is happening at all &#8212; is organized by residents through volunteer groups.</p>
<p class="n-body" style="margin:18px 0 0">Neither of those is a complaint. It does mean that the answer to &#8220;who do I call about this?&#8221; is never &#8220;the town&#8221;, and that finding the right body is the first thing a new resident has to learn. That is what this page and the community page are for.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

